-- title:
--   Rank-one LAR preprocessing and random selectors
-- statement:
--   Rank-one preprocessing converts an LAR test into a zero-fiber LWE test. This interface specifies random selectors, circuit bundles, zero-secret experiments, the computable direction used by the rank-one construction, and bounded uniform choices. It gives the data needed to represent the original distinguisher as one subroutine call.
